### Sattadhar Textile — Customers: registration + walk-in dedupe
### VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client). Run top to bottom.
###
### The point of this file is steps 5–9: the same person, reached four
### different ways, must end up as exactly ONE customer record.

@base = http://localhost:4000
@api = {{base}}/api/v1

### ─── 1. Login as ADMIN ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# @name adminLogin
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "admin", "password": "ChangeMe@123" }

###
@adminAccess = {{adminLogin.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### ─── 2. Login as STAFF ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
### kirti is seeded with `customer.create` ON.
# @name staffLogin
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "kirti", "password": "Staff@123" }

###
@staffAccess = {{staffLogin.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### ─── 3. Pick a product with stock — copy the id below ──────────────────
GET {{api}}/products?pageSize=50
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

###
@productId = <PASTE_ANY_IN_STOCK_PRODUCT_ID>

### Change this once per run so the test stays meaningful.
@testPhone = 9812345670

### ─── 4. Is the number free? ────────────────────────────────────────────
### Expect 200 with "data": null. Not a 404 — "nobody has this" is an answer.
GET {{api}}/customers/by-phone?phone={{testPhone}}
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}

### ─── 5. Register a customer (STAFF may) ────────────────────────────────
### Note the response: `phone` comes back canonicalised to +91…
# @name newCustomer
POST {{api}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}

{
  "name": "Test Kirana Stores",
  "phone": "{{testPhone}}",
  "type": "RETAIL",
  "city": "Ahmedabad",
  "state": "Gujarat"
}

###
@customerId = {{newCustomer.response.body.data.id}}

### ─── 6. The same number, typed four ways — all refused ─────────────────
### Every one expects 409 CONFLICT, and the message names who holds it.
POST {{api}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}

{ "name": "Duplicate 1", "phone": "{{testPhone}}" }

###
POST {{api}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}

{ "name": "Duplicate 2", "phone": "+91{{testPhone}}" }

###
POST {{api}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}

{ "name": "Duplicate 3", "phone": "91{{testPhone}}" }

###
### With a space in the middle, the way a phone is actually written down.
POST {{api}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}

{ "name": "Duplicate 4", "phone": "98123 45670" }

### ─── 7. Walk-in with a NEW number → registers a customer ───────────────
### Expect `walkInCustomer.outcome` = "registered" and a non-null customerId.
POST {{api}}/bills
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}

{
  "billingMode": "NON_GST",
  "walkInName": "Raghav Counter Sale",
  "walkInPhone": "9812345671",
  "items": [{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "qty": 1 }]
}

### ─── 8. Same walk-in again, typed differently → NO duplicate ───────────
### Expect `walkInCustomer.outcome` = "matched", and the SAME customerId.
POST {{api}}/bills
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}

{
  "billingMode": "NON_GST",
  "walkInName": "Raghav (typed differently)",
  "walkInPhone": "+91 98123 45671",
  "items": [{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "qty": 1 }]
}

### ─── 9. One record, both sales ─────────────────────────────────────────
### Expect exactly one customer, and two bills against them.
GET {{api}}/customers?search=9812345671
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

### ─── 10. A matched walk-in gets their REAL terms ───────────────────────
### Chirag Mehta Textiles is WHOLESALE. Billing them through the walk-in
### field must charge the wholesale rate, because the match runs BEFORE the
### rates are worked out. Compare `items[0].rate` to the product's two rates.
POST {{api}}/bills
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

{
  "billingMode": "GST",
  "walkInName": "typed at the counter",
  "walkInPhone": "+919820000001",
  "items": [{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "qty": 1 }]
}

### ─── 11. A walk-in with NO phone stays anonymous ───────────────────────
### Expect customerId null and no `walkInCustomer` key. There is nothing to
### identify a passer-by with, and inventing a record helps nobody.
POST {{api}}/bills
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}

{
  "billingMode": "NON_GST",
  "walkInName": "Passer-by",
  "items": [{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "qty": 1 }]
}

### ─── 12. Credit to an unknown number is refused ────────────────────────
### Expect 400. A freshly registered walk-in has creditLimit 0, which means
### "no limit set" — allowing khata here would hand a stranger unlimited
### credit. Register them properly first.
POST {{api}}/bills
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

{
  "billingMode": "GST",
  "walkInName": "Stranger",
  "walkInPhone": "9333300099",
  "paymentMode": "CREDIT",
  "items": [{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "qty": 1 }]
}

### ─── 13. …but a RECOGNISED customer may buy on khata ───────────────────
### Expect 201, with their own credit limit enforced.
POST {{api}}/bills
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

{
  "billingMode": "GST",
  "walkInName": "x",
  "walkInPhone": "+919820000001",
  "paymentMode": "CREDIT",
  "items": [{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "qty": 1 }]
}

### ─── 14. A failed bill leaves no customer behind ───────────────────────
### Expect 409 (not enough stock), then a null lookup: registration happens
### inside the bill transaction, so it rolls back with it.
POST {{api}}/bills
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

{
  "billingMode": "GST",
  "walkInName": "Should Not Exist",
  "walkInPhone": "9444400099",
  "items": [{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "qty": 999999 }]
}

###
GET {{api}}/customers/by-phone?phone=9444400099
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}
